{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_uunsngvbnttrxoczb3rnbtrnhekuxvnie6c3ozrgmxocnk7ujsfq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## What was translated\n\n`c_src/` turned out to be a single-file library (`src/lib.c`, 402 lines) — a subset of Randy Gaul's `cute_c2` 2D collision/raycast code. I built the C library with CMake first and ran `nm -D` to establish the definition of done: **28 exported functions**, all `T`, no exported data symbols and no namespace-renaming macros (I checked the header — only `poly_ray` is declared there, but the build exports every non-`static` function).\n\n## Completion gate\n\n`nm -D` on `libtranslation.so` vs the C `.so`: **28 vs 28, `diff` empty.** All types (`c2v`, `c2r`, `c2x`, `c2m`, `c2Circle`, `c2AABB`, `c2Capsule`, `c2Poly`, `c2Ray`, `c2Raycast`) are `#[repr(C)]` so the by-value struct ABI (SSE register pairs vs. MEMORY class for the 20-byte `c2Ray`/`c2Capsule`) matches.\n\n## Verification\n\nI wrote a differential harness that `dlopen`s both `.so`s and calls all 28 symbols through identical function pointers, comparing results with `memcmp` on raw bytes (so `-0.0` vs `+0.0` and NaN payloads count), with out-params pre-poisoned so untouched bytes are also checked. **34.2M bit-exact comparisons, 0 genuine value differences** across three input regimes: finite-only, finite+infinities, and everything including NaN.\n\nThree fidelity traps the harness caught or that needed care:\n- `c2Div` does `a * (1.0f / b)`, **not** `a / b` — different results for finite inputs.\n- The C open-codes `fabsf`/`fminf`/`fmaxf` as ternaries. `f32::abs` would turn `-0.0` into `+0.0`, and `f32::min/max` differ on NaN — so I reproduced the ternaries literally as `c_abs`/`c_min`/`c_max`.\n- `c2MulrvT`'s `-a.s * b.x` is `(-a.s) * b.x` in C (unary minus binds tighter), not `-(a.s * b.x)`.\n\nI also preserved the C's bugs/quirks rather than fixing them: `c2RaytoPoly` uses unchecked pointer indexing (a `count > 8` reads past the arrays, as in C), `c2RaytoCapsule` writes `out` before its early `return 1`, and `poly_ray` leaves `verts[4..8]` unread.\n\n## One documented divergence\n\nThe only non-matching bits are the **sign bit of a returned NaN**, and only when two NaNs meet as operands of one arithmetic op (10,317 of 11.4M cases, all NaN-payload-only, all requiring NaN *input*).\n\nI initially tried to fix this by emulating x86 SSE NaN propagation explicitly — that made things *worse* (44,571 mismatches), which sent me to the disassembly. GCC had algebraically rewritten `(-a.s) * b.x + a.c * b.y` into `subss` with the operands **reversed** (`a.c * b.y - a.s * b.x`) while leaving the sibling lane's `addss` in source order — so the two lanes of the same function propagate NaN from *opposite* operands. Matching that would mean hand-pinning register operands per instruction to one particular GCC invocation rather than translating the C, and it's unspecified by both C and IEEE-754. I reverted to the faithful source-order arithmetic and documented the reasoning in the module header. `poly_ray`, the only header-declared entry point, takes no float inputs and is byte-identical (returns `0`, leaves both out-params untouched).\n\nDeliverables are `translation/Cargo.toml` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`) and `translation/src/lib.rs`; `c_src/` is unmodified and I removed my verification scaffolding."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":376,"cache_read_input_tokens":104265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":376,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a9ecc60-f6f2-4da8-9e8d-48cb15902a44","uuid":"5c1a8948-949b-4796-a7d7-8679696b67d4","timestamp":"2026-08-27T14:08:58.480Z"}
